# `pathset` Standalone Wire Specification

A pathset is an ordered list of non-empty payment paths. Its standalone wire
payload has no field-ID or VL prefix; it is self-framed by element masks and
terminators.

| Byte / bit | Meaning | Following payload |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `01` bit | Account present | 20-byte AccountID |
| `10` bit | Currency present | 20-byte Currency |
| `20` bit | Issuer present | 20-byte AccountID |
| `FF` | Boundary between alternate paths | No payload |
| `00` | End of the entire pathset | No payload |

Mask bits may be combined, and payloads occur in account/currency/issuer
order. Unknown mask bits fail. A leading `00` or `FF` would terminate an empty
path, which the decoder rejects; the CLI therefore rejects empty JSON pathsets
instead of emitting a non-round-trippable lone `00`.

